{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"cda47f957ad5e5dd","x":-620,"y":-268,"width":1260,"height":328,"color":"2","type":"text","text":"I don't know the future. But I like somethings and I hate somethings. I want a future where I get to do more of the things that I like and less of the things that I hate. However, my choices are constrained by my general socio-politico-economic condition. And I cannot choose freely.\n\nI know there is a better way to choose. **I don't want to go back to academia**. I should be thankful for this job, because of how much free time it affords me. And I am not of the ungrateful. It is only human to want more. In fact one has a natural desire to expand their sphere of influence and it is even natural to expect your sphere of influence to expand. \n\nOne can either go with the flow or take a step. When one takes a step it changes something. It causes a perturbation. If one leaves it at that step, that perturbation gets damped and goes away. One can keep taking steps. The idea is to put yourself out there. You have to see what returns. Of course most of the time, it is 2 views or three views. I don't just want views I want engagement. I want to engage with the content that others are creating and create my own content that others engage with. I want it to be informative. I want to teach and learn. What works and what doesn't. \n\nSo the question then becomes what do you want to create? It is hard work to create. There was a time I could just write and I can still do it, but the standards have increased. You are expected to do more work. I tend to rant. \n\n\n\n\n\n"},
		{"id":"873043285b361ff5","x":-481,"y":95,"width":941,"height":245,"color":"1","type":"text","text":"What does Allah want of me? To live a happy, prosperous and grateful life while fulfilling my covenant with Allah. My strength is my writing. "}
	],
	"edges":[]
}